  "concept": {
    "movement": "An armored deep-water fish cruises with a steady heavy trunk and deliberate lateral caudal strokes. Faster travel strengthens the posterior wave while the head, eye lenses and plated torso remain coherent; pectoral fins steer rather than walk.",
    "attack": "A short backward load and forceful straight forward armored-head/body ram, with pectorals swept clear of the face. No invented jaw opening is assumed.",
    "death": "Tail propulsion fades and the fish drifts down into a supported forward rest on separate head and belly regions. Fins fold or relax clear of the bottom rather than holding the body up on a single fin tip; the natural upward tail silhouette is retained when clearance allows."
